From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] presence: publish the current shared Activity

The GTK4 presence wrapper already creates and joins the Telepathy room, but
it did not publish the owner's current Activity through BuddyInfo.  Peers
could therefore see the Salut contact while GetActivities() stayed empty.
Publish the same current-activity tuple used by the GTK3 Neighborhood model.
Failure is logged but does not turn a successful room creation into a failed
share.

--- a/src/sugar4/presence/activity.py
+++ b/src/sugar4/presence/activity.py
@@ -468,1 +468,12 @@
             self._start_tracking_channel()
+            self.telepathy_conn.SetCurrentActivity(
+                self._id,
+                self.room_handle,
+                reply_handler=lambda: _logger.debug(
+                    "%r: current Activity published", self
+                ),
+                error_handler=lambda error: _logger.warning(
+                    "%r: unable to publish current Activity: %s", self, error
+                ),
+                dbus_interface=CONN_INTERFACE_BUDDY_INFO,
+            )
             share_activity_cb(self)
         else:
             share_activity_error_cb(self, error)
